# Git hooks are executed by the OS shell, not by Python's importer: a CRLF
# checkout appends "\r" to every command, so the shebang and each hook line
# fail with "<cmd>\r: not found".  This machine uses core.autocrlf=true, which
# would otherwise rewrite these files on checkout.  Pin them to LF everywhere.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
